Say which nub is being matched, and when

The M counter said how many times probeCandidates was entered, but not which
nub it was entered for, so the panel could not tell progress from repetition:
two rounds that both said M32/2 might have been two different nubs or the
same one twice.

The line now carries the nub's name and the clock, so the panel reads as a
time-ordered list of what the kernel is matching, and a nub that comes
round twice shows up as the same name twice with the gap between the two
stamps.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
index a516193..d7d3433 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -3822,7 +3822,15 @@ IOService::probeCandidates( OSOrderedSet * matches )
 	{
 		static uint32_t nio_probe_cand;
 		if ((++nio_probe_cand & 0x0u) == 0) {
-			printf("\nM%u/%d", nio_probe_cand, matches ? matches->getCount() : -1);
+			clock_sec_t nio_sec;
+			clock_usec_t nio_usec;
+			uint32_t nio_now = 0;
+
+			clock_get_system_microtime(&nio_sec, &nio_usec);
+			nio_now = nio_usec + (uint32_t)(nio_sec % 1000) * 1000000u;
+			printf("\nM%u/%d %s %u", nio_probe_cand,
+			    matches ? matches->getCount() : -1,
+			    getName() ? getName() : "?", nio_now);
 		}
 		if (nio_probe_cand >= 200000u) {
 			panic("nio: probeCandidates entered %u times", nio_probe_cand);
